  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DIASPORA IN FOCUS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The Diaspora focus involves the (young) Ghanaian diaspora in the Netherlands. The Ghanaian community has increased steadily from over 12,000 in 1996 to close to 30,000 today (Source: Embassy of Ghana to the Netherlands, 2021). 
This element seizes the potential of the youth within this target group and their willingness to make a lasting impact in the country of their heritage. The Dutch-Ghanaian diaspora will be a benefit to private sector development in Ghana. 
This also aligns with the &#x2018;homegoing&#x2019; trend as well as &#x2018;the year of return&#x2019; in 2019, in which the Ghanaian government actively encouraged the diaspora community to return to Ghana to get in touch with their heritage. The aim of the Diaspora focus is to connect the Dutch-Ghanaian diaspora to the private sector in Ghana. 
They can contribute with their knowledge, network, and skills. Possible partners for this are the Netherlands African Business Council (NABC), African Studies Centre Leiden (ASCL), and Orange Corners Ghana. As the &#x2018;Diaspora focus&#x2019; centers around a new target group, GNBCC proposes to first conduct market research on the possible needs and wishes of the diaspora community, before initiating the other two components of the project:&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
